# graphify scope lock — keep the curated map (game code + project docs).
# Mirrors the hand-filtered scope of the initial build so `graphify --update`
# and full rebuilds don't re-scan excluded process-docs / skill packs /
# screenshots and blow the scope (and the token budget) wide open.
# gitignore syntax; merged with .gitignore, .graphifyignore wins on conflict.
# See CLAUDE.md "Knowledge graph" for the scope rationale.

# graphify's own outputs — never graph the map of the map
graphify-out/

# OpenSpec change-workflow process artifacts (~141 files) — planning history,
# not how the game works. The capability CONTRACTS in openspec/specs/ ARE kept.
openspec/changes/

# Generic three.js skill packs — upstream reference docs, not project code.
.claude/skills/

# Images: skip PWA icons, character art, and proof-of-work screenshots; keep
# only the real architecture diagram that was in the curated build.
*.png
*.svg
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
!zerble-festival-architecture.png
